\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TSVagr0
\item[* relevant examples:]
x1 comprar x2 $\rightarrow$\\
x1 comprar x2
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoClause
\item[* class:] TC:TSVagr
\item[* date of creation:] 18-mar-1988 12:30:00  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster
\item[* copied from:] Jan Odijk
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To let non finite clauses pass the subject verb agreement TC
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
The following Subject-Verb Agreement transformations have been made:
\begin{enumerate}
\item {\bf TSVagr0} \\
default for infinite clauses.
\item {\bf TSVagr1} \\
SV-agreement for the following categories in subject-position:\\
- subrule1: NPVAR \\
- subrule2: CNVAR \\
- subrule3: PRONP \\
- subrule4: NP (NPhead = redelloNP, redellosNP, eseNP, esteNP, aquelNP) \\
- subrule5: PRONPVAR (i.e. ergatives with post-verbal subject)
\item {\bf TSVagr2} \\
ser/estar + ADJ, again with 5 subrules.
\item {\bf TSVagr3} \\
Passive: PRONPVAR + [ ser + PtcPas ]
\end{enumerate}
{\bf NB.} No rule is made for "estar + PtcPas". \\ 
For the moment this type of construction can only be handled if the "PtcPas" 
is (also) an ADJ.
\end{description}


